       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in many labels. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the typical maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, in some other schedule\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order saying the dose was verified."
